      "message": "inline routes package into backend\n\nCollapses packages/routes/ into backend/routes/. The routes factories\nare now a local import instead of a published npm package — reflects\npost-K8s reality where this app's own backend is the only consumer.\n\nSide effects:\n- Drop the @nelsong6/*-routes dependency from backend/package.json\n- Remove publish-routes.yml workflow\n- Simplify Dockerfile: drop GitHub Packages auth scaffolding\n- Drop `packages: read` permission + NPM_TOKEN build arg from build-and-deploy\n- Update CLAUDE.md architecture sections\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
